    "content": "<h5>Desolate Echo</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>SP Cost:</strong> 80<br><br><strong>Start SP:</strong> 30<br><br><strong>Charging:</strong> Automatic<br><br><strong>Activation:</strong> Action<br><br><strong>Duration:</strong> 5 Rounds</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">As part of using this Skill, you may cast an Art with a Casting Time of an Action. After you have cast that Art, an Echo appears within 5 feet of a Creature affected by the original Art (your choice if there are multiple Creatures). The Echo is a visible but intangible orb of Originium Arts. When a hostile Creature enters a 20-foot-radius around the Echo, and is not behind Full Cover from the Echo , they must make a Strength Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC. On a failed Save, they take 6d6 Damage, with the Damage Type being one of the Damage Types present on the original Art (your choice), are pulled 15 feet towards the Echo, and have their Movement Speed reduced by half (rounding down). On a successful Save, they take half as much Damage, and suffer no other effects. A Creature only needs to make this Save once per Turn.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Source:</strong> AK5e 1st Edition v1.3.1, Chapter 3: Caster / Elite Caster Skills</p>",
    "rawSource": "| Desolate Echo\t| 80\t | 30\t| Automatic\t| Action\t| As part of using this Skill, you may cast an Art with a Casting Time of an Action. After you have cast that Art, an Echo appears within 5 feet of a Creature affected by the original Art (your choice if there are multiple Creatures). The Echo is a visible but intangible orb of Originium Arts. When a hostile Creature enters a 20-foot-radius around the Echo, and is not behind Full Cover from the Echo , they must make a Strength Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC. On a failed Save, they take 6d6 Damage, with the Damage Type being one of the Damage Types present on the original Art (your choice), are pulled 15 feet towards the Echo, and have their Movement Speed reduced by half (rounding down). On a successful Save, they take half as much Damage, and suffer no other effects. A Creature only needs to make this Save once per Turn.\t| 5 Rounds"
