    "itemType": "feat",
    "level": null,
    "systemData": {},
    "content": "<h4>Basic Brawling Techniques</h4>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">The Techniques available to the Brawler Branch are listed in alphabetical order. All Brawling Techniques are considered to be applications of your Press the Attack Feature.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Body Check (1 Aggression)</strong> <br><br>When you hit a Creature with an Unarmed Strike, you may use this Technique (no Action required) to attempt to Shove that Creature. On a success, the distance you shove that Creature is doubled.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Cross Counter (1 Aggression)</strong><br><br>When a Creature makes a Melee Attack against you, you can use this Technique as a Reaction to increase your Armour Class by a value equal to your Proficiency Bonus against that Attack, possibly causing it to miss. If that Attack misses you, you can make an Unarmed Attack against that Creature as part of this Reaction.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Feint (1 Aggression)</strong><br><br>You may use this Technique as an Bonus Action; choose one Creature within your Reach; your next Unarmed Strike against this Creature before the end of your next Turn is made at Advantage.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Follow Up (1 Aggression)</strong><br><br>When you hit a Creature with an Unarmed Strike, you can use this Technique (no Action required) to make an Unarmed Strike against the same Creature. You can only use this Technique once per Turn.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Footwork (1 Aggression)</strong><br><br>After making a Melee Attack, you can use this Technique (no Action required) to move up to half of your Movement Speed. This Movement does not provoke Opportunity Attacks.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Guard Up (1 Aggression)</strong><br><br>You may use this Technique as a Bonus Action; you take the Dodge Action as part of that Bonus Action.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Slip Off (2 Aggression)</strong><br><br>When you would take Damage from an Attack you can see, you can use this Technique as a Reaction to halve that Attack’s Damage against you.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Tag In (2 Aggression)</strong><br><br>If there is a Willing Creature (that is not Incapacitated) within your Reach, you may use this Technique to swap positions with them. This Movement still requires you to spend Movement, and does not provoke Opportunity Attacks.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">Additionally, either you or the Creature you swapped with (your choice) may then make a single Melee Attack against a valid target.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">You may only use Tag In once per Turn.</p>",
    "rawSource": "#### Basic Brawling Techniques\nThe Techniques available to the Brawler Branch are listed in alphabetical order. All Brawling Techniques are considered to be applications of your Press the Attack Feature.\n\n <img \n  src='https://arknights.wiki.gg/images/Flint.png?9dc029' \n  style='position:absolute;top:130px;right:170px;width:820px' />\n\n\\column\n\n**Body Check (1 Aggression)** <br>\nWhen you hit a Creature with an Unarmed Strike, you may use this Technique (no Action required) to attempt to Shove that Creature. On a success, the distance you shove that Creature is doubled.\n:\n\n**Cross Counter (1 Aggression)**<br>\nWhen a Creature makes a Melee Attack against you, you can use this Technique as a Reaction to increase your Armour Class by a value equal to your Proficiency Bonus against that Attack, possibly causing it to miss. If that Attack misses you, you can make an Unarmed Attack against that Creature as part of this Reaction.\n:\n**Feint (1 Aggression)**<br>\nYou may use this Technique as an Bonus Action; choose one Creature within your Reach; your next Unarmed Strike against this Creature before the end of your next Turn is made at Advantage.\n:\n**Follow Up (1 Aggression)**<br>\nWhen you hit a Creature with an Unarmed Strike, you can use this Technique (no Action required) to make an Unarmed Strike against the same Creature. You can only use this Technique once per Turn.\n:\n**Footwork (1 Aggression)**<br>\nAfter making a Melee Attack, you can use this Technique (no Action required) to move up to half of your Movement Speed. This Movement does not provoke Opportunity Attacks.\n:\n**Guard Up (1 Aggression)**<br>\nYou may use this Technique as a Bonus Action; you take the Dodge Action as part of that Bonus Action.\n:\n**Slip Off (2 Aggression)**<br>\nWhen you would take Damage from an Attack you can see, you can use this Technique as a Reaction to halve that Attack’s Damage against you.\n:\n**Tag In (2 Aggression)**<br>\nIf there is a Willing Creature (that is not Incapacitated) within your Reach, you may use this Technique to swap positions with them. This Movement still requires you to spend Movement, and does not provoke Opportunity Attacks. \n:\nAdditionally, either you or the Creature you swapped with (your choice) may then make a single Melee Attack against a valid target.\n:\nYou may only use Tag In once per Turn.\n\n{{pageNumber,auto}}  \n\\page"
