    "content": "<h4>1st Level: Essence of the Liberator</h4>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">You take action only when the moment is right. Until then, you watch and wait, providing what succor you can to those who rally to you. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Liberty.</strong> You have a special resource called Liberty. Liberty is expended to fuel your other Features, and empower your Operator Skills. Your maximum Liberty is 6.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">You can generate Liberty in the following ways. You can only generate Liberty during Combat.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• You gain 1 Liberty at the end of any of your Turns that you did not:</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• Activate an Operator Skill, or have an active Operator Skill.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• Cast an Art.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• Make an Attack Roll.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• You gain 1 Liberty when you use your Guide the Masses Feature as an Action.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Guide the Masses.</strong> As an Action while in Combat, you can choose an allied Creature you can see within 20 feet, and grant them one of the following bonuses (your choice) until the beginning of your next Turn; these effects are not cumulative.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• <strong>Advocate.</strong> The next time that Creature gains Hit Points or Temporary Hit Points, they gain an additional amount equal to your twice Proficiency Bonus or twice your current Liberty, whichever is higher.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• <strong>Empower.</strong> That Creature gains Damage Reduction against the next Damage they take equal to your Proficiency Bonus or your current Liberty, whichever is higher.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• <strong>Uplift.</strong> That Creature's next successful Attack deals additional Damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus or your current Liberty, whichever is higher.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">Starting at 7th Level, if you have used this Feature as an Action during a Turn, you may also use it as a Bonus Action during that Turn, but you must choose a different Creature for that Bonus Action.</p>",
    "rawSource": "#### 1st Level: Essence of the Liberator\nYou take action only when the moment is right. Until then, you watch and wait, providing what succor you can to those who rally to you. You gain the following benefits:\n:\n**Liberty.** You have a special resource called Liberty. Liberty is expended to fuel your other Features, and empower your Operator Skills. Your maximum Liberty is 6.\n:\nYou can generate Liberty in the following ways. You can only generate Liberty during Combat.\n- You gain 1 Liberty at the end of any of your Turns that you did not:\n  - Activate an Operator Skill, or have an active Operator Skill.\n  - Cast an Art.\n  - Make an Attack Roll.\n- You gain 1 Liberty when you use your Guide the Masses Feature as an Action.\n\n{{align-text:left\n**Guide the Masses.** As an Action while in Combat, you can choose an allied Creature you can see within 20 feet, and grant them one of the following bonuses (your choice) until the beginning of your next Turn; these effects are not cumulative. \n- **Advocate.** The next time that Creature gains Hit Points or Temporary Hit Points, they gain an additional amount equal to your twice Proficiency Bonus or twice your current Liberty, whichever is higher.\n- **Empower.** That Creature gains Damage Reduction against the next Damage they take equal to your Proficiency Bonus or your current Liberty, whichever is higher.\n- **Uplift.** That Creature's next successful Attack deals additional Damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus or your current Liberty, whichever is higher.\n}}\n\n{{align-text:left\nStarting at 7th Level, if you have used this Feature as an Action during a Turn, you may also use it as a Bonus Action during that Turn, but you must choose a different Creature for that Bonus Action.\n}}\n\n\\column"
