    "rawSource": "#### 1st Level: Art of War\nIn your hands, all but the heaviest weapons flow like wind, and cut like water. You gain the following benefits:\n\n**Additional Fighting Styles.** You gain a Fighting Style available to the Guard or Marksman Class. Whenever you complete a Long Rest, you may exchange this Fighting Style for a different one.\n\n**Additional Weapon Proficiencies.** You are Proficient in all Light Ranged and Heavy Ranged Weapons.\n\n**Martial Mastery.** Your Proficiency with all kinds of weapons provides you with a versatility in their use unavailable to the layman. Weapons that you are wielding, and are Proficient with, gain additional benefits according to the Martial Mastery Table.  \n\n##### Martial Mastery\n| Mastery Property  | Affected Weapons | Additional Effect |\n|:-----------------:|:----------------:|:-----------------:|\n| Can Opener        | Crossbow, Hammer, Heavy Crossbow, Heavy Hammer, Rifle | When you hit a Creature that has Physical DR, that Attack deals an additional 1d6 Damage. | \n| Cornering         | Bow, Greatbow, Machine Gun, Nailgun | When you hit a Creature, that Creature's Speed is reduced by 5 feet until the end of their next Turn. \n| Drive             | Spear, Polearm, Whip        | When you hit a Creature, you can move that Creature up to 10 feet in a direction of your choice; this movement does not provoke Opportunity Attacks.\n| Executioner       | Knife, Shotgun   | When you hit a Creature that has the Incapacitated or Prone Condition, that Attack deals an additional 2d6 Damage. |\n| Flourish          | Sword, Greatsword, Heavy Throwing Disc, Throwing Disc | When you make an Attack with this Weapon and miss, you may roll 1d6 and add the total to your result, potentially turning that miss into hit. Once you have hit as a result of this Feature, you may not do so again until the start of your next Turn. \n| Lethality         | Axe, Greataxe, Hand Crossbow, Handgun | When you hit a Creature that does not have any Physical DR, that attack deals an additional 1d6 Damage. |\n\n\\column"
