    "rawSource": "#### 1st Level: Siege Mode\nAt the beginning of your Turn you may declare that you will enter Siege Mode (no Action required) until the end of that Turn. While in Siege Mode, your Speed is reduced to 0 (and cannot be increased), and you have Disadvantage on Ranged Weapon Attacks against Creatures within 20ft of you. However, you gain the following benefits:\n\n**Additional Damage.** Your Attacks deal 1d8 additional Damage.\n\n**Crushing Shots.** While they are Equipped by you, Ranged Weapons gain the Crush (X) Property, where X is equal to twice your Proficiency Bonus. If it already has the Crush (X) Property, add the values of X together and use that value for X.\n\n**Ignore Brace.** You ignore the effects of the Brace Property.\n\n**Long Range Shooting.** You suffer no penalty for Attacking at Long Range."
