    "content": "<h4>4th Level: Intravenous Line</h4>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">You gain an additional way to use your Life Support Feature:</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Intravenous Line.</strong> As an Action, you can expend 10 Life Support to choose a Creature you can see within 15 feet, and tune your Arts to that Creature's biorhythms for 10 minutes, or until you use this Feature again. An unwilling Creature must make a Constitution Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC, being affected by this feature on a failed Save, or taking 2d8 Necrotic Damage on a successful Save.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">While tuned to a Creature, you know the direction that Creature is in, and you can sense when it has less than half of its maximum Hit Points. In addition, once per Turn, when you deal Damage or restore Hit Points to that Creature, roll 1d6; the amount restored or dealt is increased by the amount rolled.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">This amount is increased to 2d6 at Level 7.</p>",
    "rawSource": "#### 4th Level: Intravenous Line\nYou gain an additional way to use your Life Support Feature:\n\n**Intravenous Line.** As an Action, you can expend 10 Life Support to choose a Creature you can see within 15 feet, and tune your Arts to that Creature's biorhythms for 10 minutes, or until you use this Feature again. An unwilling Creature must make a Constitution Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC, being affected by this feature on a failed Save, or taking 2d8 Necrotic Damage on a successful Save. \n:\nWhile tuned to a Creature, you know the direction that Creature is in, and you can sense when it has less than half of its maximum Hit Points. In addition, once per Turn, when you deal Damage or restore Hit Points to that Creature, roll 1d6; the amount restored or dealt is increased by the amount rolled. \n:\nThis amount is increased to 2d6 at Level 7."
