    "content": "<h5>Protocol: Soaring Dragon</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>SP Cost:</strong> 50<br><br><strong>Start SP:</strong> 15<br><br><strong>Charging:</strong> Automatic<br><br><strong>Activation:</strong> Action<br><br><strong>Duration:</strong> Instant</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">You create an Air Supporter Automaton (Page 466) at a location you can see within 10 feet. You control this Automaton as if you were an Artificer (See the Artificer Supporter's Master of Machines Feature); this Automaton does not count against the maximum number of Automatons you can control. The Automaton you create in this way can only take the following Action, as an Action; this Automaton chooses a location it can see within 100 feet. All Creatures within 10 feet of that location must make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your Martial DC or Spell Save DC (your choice). On a failed Save, they take 3d6 Thunder Damage; on a successful Save, they take half as much Damage. After 1 minute, the Automaton you created in this way self-destructs.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Source:</strong> AK5e 1st Edition v1.3.1, Chapter 3: Supporter / Advanced Supporter Skills Continued</p>",
