    "rawSources": [
      "##### AEGIS System\n**Effect:** This Automaton possess a powerful Originium Arts inhibiting barrier; Creatures within a 10 foot radius sphere centred on this Automaton have Advantage on Saving Throws against Arts that originate from outside of this radius.",
      "#### 4th Level: Heavy Duty Upgrades\nRefining of your craft has allowed you to produce upgraded versions of the typical Automatons. You gain the following benefits:\n\n**Basic Personality Matrix.** You can instill a rudimentary sentience whenever you create a new custom Automaton, or as a Short Rest Activity with a pre-existing custom Automaton. It can speak, understands that it is artificial, and is unwaveringly loyal to you. When you instil sentience, roll a d6 on the following table to determine its personality:\n\n##### Machine Personality\n| Roll | Personality |\n|:----:|:-----------:|\n| 1    | Taciturn    |\n| 2    | Caring      |\n| 3    | Excitable   |\n| 4    | Warlike     |\n| 5    | Nervous     |\n| 6    | Analytic    |\n\n**Loaded for Bear.** When you create a new custom Automaton, or use your Fort Builder Feature, you may apply one of the Upgrades, detailed below, based on whether you create a Automaton or Portable Cover.\n:\nAdditionally, as a Long Rest Activity, you can install one Upgrade onto each of your Automatons; the maximum number of Upgrades an Automaton can have is two.",
      "{{note\n##### Artificer DC\nSome of the Heavy Duty Upgrades call for your Artificer DC; this is calculated as 8 + your Intelligence Modifier + your Proficiency Bonus. Additionally, when you would use your Martial DC, you can use your Artificer DC instead.\n}}"
    ],
    "classOption": {
      "category": "upgrade",
      "target": "Automaton",
      "effect": "##### AEGIS System\n**Effect:** This Automaton possess a powerful Originium Arts inhibiting barrier; Creatures within a 10 foot radius sphere centred on this Automaton have Advantage on Saving Throws against Arts that originate from outside of this radius."
    },
    "ruleContext": "#### 4th Level: Heavy Duty Upgrades\nRefining of your craft has allowed you to produce upgraded versions of the typical Automatons. You gain the following benefits:\n\n**Basic Personality Matrix.** You can instill a rudimentary sentience whenever you create a new custom Automaton, or as a Short Rest Activity with a pre-existing custom Automaton. It can speak, understands that it is artificial, and is unwaveringly loyal to you. When you instil sentience, roll a d6 on the following table to determine its personality:\n\n##### Machine Personality\n| Roll | Personality |\n|:----:|:-----------:|\n| 1    | Taciturn    |\n| 2    | Caring      |\n| 3    | Excitable   |\n| 4    | Warlike     |\n| 5    | Nervous     |\n| 6    | Analytic    |\n\n**Loaded for Bear.** When you create a new custom Automaton, or use your Fort Builder Feature, you may apply one of the Upgrades, detailed below, based on whether you create a Automaton or Portable Cover.\n:\nAdditionally, as a Long Rest Activity, you can install one Upgrade onto each of your Automatons; the maximum number of Upgrades an Automaton can have is two.\n\n{{note\n##### Artificer DC\nSome of the Heavy Duty Upgrades call for your Artificer DC; this is calculated as 8 + your Intelligence Modifier + your Proficiency Bonus. Additionally, when you would use your Martial DC, you can use your Artificer DC instead.\n}}"
