    "itemType": "feat",
    "level": null,
    "systemData": {},
    "content": "<h5>Finish Them (3 Acumen)</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">You command for an allied Creature to bring a swift and violent end to a foe. Choose an allied Creature that is within 5 feet of a hostile Creature that is either Prone, or has no Speeds above 0. The allied Creature can make a Weapon Attack against the hostile Creature; Ranged Attacks are not made at Disadvantage for the Creature being Prone, or for making an Ranged Attack while there is a Creature within 5 feet. If it hits, do not roll Damage for that Attack; instead, it deals the maximum possible Damage, and ignores any Damage Reduction on the target.</p>\n<h3>Rule context</h3>\n<h4>1st Level: Tactical Knowledge</h4>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">Your training as a Tactician allows you to direct the battlefield in ways others cannot; you gain access to Basic Tactics (detailed below) that are fueled by your Acumen.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Acumen:</strong> Acumen is the resource that represents your capacity to bear the mental strain of commanding. Your maximum Acumen is equal to twice your Proficiency Bonus. You regain all expended Acumen when you complete a Long Rest.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Using Tactics:</strong> You can activate a Tactic either as an Action or a Bonus Action by expending the required Acumen for that Tactic; this means that you can activate two Tactics in the same Turn if you have the Acumen. However, once you have used a Tactic, you cannot use that Tactic again until the start of your next Turn.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Recieving the benefit of Tactics.</strong> Many Tactics have no defined range of effect. However, a Creature must be able to hear or see the Tactician clearly to be a valid beneficiary of that Tactic; if an allied Creature is ruled by the DM as being unable to see or hear you clearly, they are not affected by your Tactics even if they are within its affected area. This means that communication through a radio, or through some other remote means, is sufficient for many Tactics to be effective. However, waving from the horizon is not likely to be clear enough to communicate your Tactics.</p>\n<aside class=\"ak5e-note\">\n<h5>Example: Delivering Tactics</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• The Tactician, Player A, is communicating with Player B, a Guard, through the use of Messenger Kits. Because Player B can hear Player A's instructions clearly, they can benefit when Player A uses the \"Fall Back\" Tactic on them.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• Player A wants to issue the \"Volley Fire\" Tactic to Players C and D, Marksmen on a nearby roof. Players C and D do not have Messenger Kits, nor can they hear Player A, but they are close enough to easily visually make out Player A's signalling with their arm, and can this benefit from that Tactic.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• Player A wants to issue the \"Move Up\" Tactic to Player E, a Caster who is 300 feet away. Player E is too far away to hear Player A's voice, does not have any other way to hear Player A, and while they can technically see them, they are so far away that they cannot make out any individual gesture. They cannot benefit from this Tactic.</p>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">From 4th Level, when a Creature expends a Reaction in response to one of your Tactics while they are within your Strategic Zone, you may immediately use your Tip of the Spear Feature on that Creature regardless of range (no Action required).</p>\n<h4>13th Level: Master Tactician</h4>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">Your mind is as great a weapon as any steel, and has laid low more enemies than most weapons will ever. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Tactical Expansion.</strong> You gain access to the Advanced Tactics listed below.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Well-Drilled.</strong> When an allied Creature begins its Turn within one of your Strategic Zones, it gains a additional Reaction that it can only expend on your Strategies or Tactics.</p>\n<aside class=\"ak5e-note\">\n<h5>Tactics for Casters</h5>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">In the world of Terra, Casters are an important part of battle tactica, no more or less than other warriors. For the Tactician's Tactics, this is represented in the following way: when a Tactic would allow a Creature to make a Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack as part of that Tactic, that Creature can instead cast a Cantrip that involves making a Melee or Ranged Spell Attack, respectively, to replace that Melee or Ranged Attack. However, if they do so, the exertion leaves them wobbling; they are Dazed until the end of their next Turn.</p>\n</aside>",
    "rawSource": "##### Finish Them (3 Acumen)\nYou command for an allied Creature to bring a swift and violent end to a foe. Choose an allied Creature that is within 5 feet of a hostile Creature that is either Prone, or has no Speeds above 0. The allied Creature can make a Weapon Attack against the hostile Creature; Ranged Attacks are not made at Disadvantage for the Creature being Prone, or for making an Ranged Attack while there is a Creature within 5 feet. If it hits, do not roll Damage for that Attack; instead, it deals the maximum possible Damage, and ignores any Damage Reduction on the target.",
