    "systemData": {},
    "classOption": {
      "category": "technique",
      "tier": "Advanced",
      "cost": "2 Aggression",
      "effect": "When you are Grappling a Creature no more than one Size Category larger than you, you may use this Technique as an Action. That Creature must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw against your Martial DC or become Restrained by you. When you Restrain a Creature in this way, you swing them around to face a direction of your choice; you are considered to be in Three-Quarters Cover against Attacks from that direction, and if an Attack against you from that direction misses, it hits the Restrained Creature instead. You may change the direction in which you are presenting the Restrained Creature as an Action during your Turn. The Restrained Creature may reattempt the Saving Throw as an Action during their Turn, ending the Condition and the Grapple on a success. You may not Attack a Creature you have Restrained in this way."
    },
    "ruleContext": "#### 1st Level: Press the Attack\nAs a Guard, you are the mainstay in any assault. Others defend, others facilitate, you push onwards. You gain access to special Press the Attack options, and gain additional ones from your Branch, that are fuelled by your Aggression.\n:\n**Aggression:** You have 4 Aggression, which you expend to use Press the Attack options. You recover all expended Aggression when you complete a Short or Long Rest.\n:\nYou gain 2 additional Aggression at 7th Level (total of 6), and at 14th Level (total of 8).\n:\n**Expending Aggression:** Each Press the Attack option dictates the circumstances in which you can use it, and how much Aggression is required to use it. Some options allow you to spend more than the minimum Aggression to amplify the effects. \n:\n****Press the Attack: Forestall (1-3 Aggression)****\nYou can use this Press the Attack Option as a Reaction when you are hit by an Attack; for each Aggression you expend, your Armour Class is increased by a value equal to your Proficiency Bonus against the triggering Attack, possibly causing it to miss. \n:\n****Press the Attack: Smite (1-3 Aggression)****\nYou can use this Press the Attack Option when you hit with an Attack (no Action required); for each Aggression you expend, that Attack deals additional Damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus.\n:\n****Press the Attack: Strike True (1-3 Aggression)****\nYou can use this Press the Attack Option when you make an Attack Roll (no Action required); for each Aggression you expend, you gain a bonus to that Attack Roll equal to your Proficiency Bonus.\n\n#### 10th Level: No Ordinary Pugilist\nYou are no back alley thug. Your hands and feet are phantasmagoric; an express pass to unconsciousness. You gain the following benefits:\n\n**Always Ready.** At the beginning of your Turn during combat, you regain one expended Aggression.\n\n**Master Brawler.** You gain access to the Advanced Brawling Techniques listed below.\n\n\\column\n\nThe Techniques available to the Brawler Branch are listed in alphabetical order. All Brawling Techniques are considered to be applications of your Press the Attack Feature.\n\n <img \n  src='https://arknights.wiki.gg/images/Flint.png?9dc029' \n  style='position:absolute;top:130px;right:170px;width:820px' />\n\n\\column\n\n#### Advanced Brawling Techniques",
    "contentVersion": "0.3.8",
    "content": "<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Human Shield (2 Aggression)</strong><br><br>When you are Grappling a Creature no more than one Size Category larger than you, you may use this Technique as an Action. That Creature must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw against your Martial DC or become Restrained by you. When you Restrain a Creature in this way, you swing them around to face a direction of your choice; you are considered to be in Three-Quarters Cover against Attacks from that direction, and if an Attack against you from that direction misses, it hits the Restrained Creature instead. You may change the direction in which you are presenting the Restrained Creature as an Action during your Turn. The Restrained Creature may reattempt the Saving Throw as an Action during their Turn, ending the Condition and the Grapple on a success. You may not Attack a Creature you have Restrained in this way.</p>\n<h3>Rule context</h3>\n<h4>1st Level: Press the Attack</h4>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">As a Guard, you are the mainstay in any assault. Others defend, others facilitate, you push onwards. You gain access to special Press the Attack options, and gain additional ones from your Branch, that are fuelled by your Aggression.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Aggression:</strong> You have 4 Aggression, which you expend to use Press the Attack options. You recover all expended Aggression when you complete a Short or Long Rest.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">You gain 2 additional Aggression at 7th Level (total of 6), and at 14th Level (total of 8).</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Expending Aggression:</strong> Each Press the Attack option dictates the circumstances in which you can use it, and how much Aggression is required to use it. Some options allow you to spend more than the minimum Aggression to amplify the effects.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Press the Attack: Forestall (1-3 Aggression)</strong><br>You can use this Press the Attack Option as a Reaction when you are hit by an Attack; for each Aggression you expend, your Armour Class is increased by a value equal to your Proficiency Bonus against the triggering Attack, possibly causing it to miss.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Press the Attack: Smite (1-3 Aggression)</strong><br>You can use this Press the Attack Option when you hit with an Attack (no Action required); for each Aggression you expend, that Attack deals additional Damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Press the Attack: Strike True (1-3 Aggression)</strong><br>You can use this Press the Attack Option when you make an Attack Roll (no Action required); for each Aggression you expend, you gain a bonus to that Attack Roll equal to your Proficiency Bonus.</p>\n<h4>10th Level: No Ordinary Pugilist</h4>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">You are no back alley thug. Your hands and feet are phantasmagoric; an express pass to unconsciousness. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Always Ready.</strong> At the beginning of your Turn during combat, you regain one expended Aggression.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Master Brawler.</strong> You gain access to the Advanced Brawling Techniques listed below.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">The Techniques available to the Brawler Branch are listed in alphabetical order. All Brawling Techniques are considered to be applications of your Press the Attack Feature.</p>\n<h4>Advanced Brawling Techniques</h4>",
    "rawSource": "**Human Shield (2 Aggression)**<br>\nWhen you are Grappling a Creature no more than one Size Category larger than you, you may use this Technique as an Action. That Creature must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw against your Martial DC or become Restrained by you. When you Restrain a Creature in this way, you swing them around to face a direction of your choice; you are considered to be in Three-Quarters Cover against Attacks from that direction, and if an Attack against you from that direction misses, it hits the Restrained Creature instead. You may change the direction in which you are presenting the Restrained Creature as an Action during your Turn. The Restrained Creature may reattempt the Saving Throw as an Action during their Turn, ending the Condition and the Grapple on a success. You may not Attack a Creature you have Restrained in this way.\n:",
