      "#### 1st Level: Press the Attack\nAs a Guard, you are the mainstay in any assault. Others defend, others facilitate, you push onwards. You gain access to special Press the Attack options, and gain additional ones from your Branch, that are fuelled by your Aggression.\n:\n**Aggression:** You have 4 Aggression, which you expend to use Press the Attack options. You recover all expended Aggression when you complete a Short or Long Rest.\n:\nYou gain 2 additional Aggression at 7th Level (total of 6), and at 14th Level (total of 8).\n:\n**Expending Aggression:** Each Press the Attack option dictates the circumstances in which you can use it, and how much Aggression is required to use it. Some options allow you to spend more than the minimum Aggression to amplify the effects. \n:\n****Press the Attack: Forestall (1-3 Aggression)****\nYou can use this Press the Attack Option as a Reaction when you are hit by an Attack; for each Aggression you expend, your Armour Class is increased by a value equal to your Proficiency Bonus against the triggering Attack, possibly causing it to miss. \n:\n****Press the Attack: Smite (1-3 Aggression)****\nYou can use this Press the Attack Option when you hit with an Attack (no Action required); for each Aggression you expend, that Attack deals additional Damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus.\n:\n****Press the Attack: Strike True (1-3 Aggression)****\nYou can use this Press the Attack Option when you make an Attack Roll (no Action required); for each Aggression you expend, you gain a bonus to that Attack Roll equal to your Proficiency Bonus.",
