    "ruleContext": "#### 1st Level: Singular Foe\nAs a Duellist, you single out your foes before utterly dismantling them with precise strikes. You gain the following benefits:\n\n**Duelling Blades.** Greatswords and Polearms are considered to have the Finesse Property while wielded by you. \n\n**Rules of Engagement.** As a Bonus Action, you may declare a hostile Creature you can see to be your Opponent. While you have an Opponent, you can earn Points in your duel with that Opponent; you can earn Points in the following ways, up to a maximum of 10:\n- +1 Point when you declare your Opponent. Once you have gained Points in this way, you cannot do so again until the end of your next Turn.\n  - You gain an additional Point if you are not wielding a Heavy Melee Weapon; this additional Point is lost if you equip a Heavy Melee Weapon after gaining the Point.\n- +1 Point at the beginning of your Turn if you have dealt Damage to your Opponent since the beginning of your last Turn. \n  - You gain an additional Point if your Opponent has NOT dealt Damage to you since your last Turn.\n\n{{align-text:left\nWhen your Opponent is reduced to 0 Hit Points, you accept their surrender, a minute passes without either of you dealing Damage to the other, or you declare a new Opponent, you lose all Points you have earned.\n:\nYou can expend your Points to carry out Engagements, detailed below. You cannot use the same Engagement more than once per Turn.\n}}\n\n#### Engagements\nThe Engagements available to the Duellist Branch are listed in alphabetical order.\n:",
    "contentVersion": "0.3.8",
    "content": "<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>En Garde (1 Point)</strong> When you expend your Reaction for your Lightning Reflexes or Reposte Press the Attack Option, you may use this Engagement (no Action required) to returning to a guarding stance, refunding use of your Reaction.</p>\n<h3>Rule context</h3>\n<h4>1st Level: Singular Foe</h4>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">As a Duellist, you single out your foes before utterly dismantling them with precise strikes. You gain the following benefits:</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Duelling Blades.</strong> Greatswords and Polearms are considered to have the Finesse Property while wielded by you.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\"><strong>Rules of Engagement.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you may declare a hostile Creature you can see to be your Opponent. While you have an Opponent, you can earn Points in your duel with that Opponent; you can earn Points in the following ways, up to a maximum of 10:</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• +1 Point when you declare your Opponent. Once you have gained Points in this way, you cannot do so again until the end of your next Turn.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• You gain an additional Point if you are not wielding a Heavy Melee Weapon; this additional Point is lost if you equip a Heavy Melee Weapon after gaining the Point.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• +1 Point at the beginning of your Turn if you have dealt Damage to your Opponent since the beginning of your last Turn.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">• You gain an additional Point if your Opponent has NOT dealt Damage to you since your last Turn.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">When your Opponent is reduced to 0 Hit Points, you accept their surrender, a minute passes without either of you dealing Damage to the other, or you declare a new Opponent, you lose all Points you have earned.</p>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">You can expend your Points to carry out Engagements, detailed below. You cannot use the same Engagement more than once per Turn.</p>\n<h4>Engagements</h4>\n<p class=\"ak5e-source-paragraph\">The Engagements available to the Duellist Branch are listed in alphabetical order.</p>",
    "rawSource": "**En Garde (1 Point)** When you expend your Reaction for your Lightning Reflexes or Reposte Press the Attack Option, you may use this Engagement (no Action required) to returning to a guarding stance, refunding use of your Reaction.\n:",
    "rawSources": [
      "**En Garde (1 Point)** When you expend your Reaction for your Lightning Reflexes or Reposte Press the Attack Option, you may use this Engagement (no Action required) to returning to a guarding stance, refunding use of your Reaction.\n:",
      "#### 1st Level: Singular Foe\nAs a Duellist, you single out your foes before utterly dismantling them with precise strikes. You gain the following benefits:\n\n**Duelling Blades.** Greatswords and Polearms are considered to have the Finesse Property while wielded by you. \n\n**Rules of Engagement.** As a Bonus Action, you may declare a hostile Creature you can see to be your Opponent. While you have an Opponent, you can earn Points in your duel with that Opponent; you can earn Points in the following ways, up to a maximum of 10:\n- +1 Point when you declare your Opponent. Once you have gained Points in this way, you cannot do so again until the end of your next Turn.\n  - You gain an additional Point if you are not wielding a Heavy Melee Weapon; this additional Point is lost if you equip a Heavy Melee Weapon after gaining the Point.\n- +1 Point at the beginning of your Turn if you have dealt Damage to your Opponent since the beginning of your last Turn. \n  - You gain an additional Point if your Opponent has NOT dealt Damage to you since your last Turn.\n\n{{align-text:left\nWhen your Opponent is reduced to 0 Hit Points, you accept their surrender, a minute passes without either of you dealing Damage to the other, or you declare a new Opponent, you lose all Points you have earned.\n:\nYou can expend your Points to carry out Engagements, detailed below. You cannot use the same Engagement more than once per Turn.\n}}",
      "#### Engagements\nThe Engagements available to the Duellist Branch are listed in alphabetical order.\n:"
    ],
    "contextSources": [
      "#### 1st Level: Singular Foe\nAs a Duellist, you single out your foes before utterly dismantling them with precise strikes. You gain the following benefits:\n\n**Duelling Blades.** Greatswords and Polearms are considered to have the Finesse Property while wielded by you. \n\n**Rules of Engagement.** As a Bonus Action, you may declare a hostile Creature you can see to be your Opponent. While you have an Opponent, you can earn Points in your duel with that Opponent; you can earn Points in the following ways, up to a maximum of 10:\n- +1 Point when you declare your Opponent. Once you have gained Points in this way, you cannot do so again until the end of your next Turn.\n  - You gain an additional Point if you are not wielding a Heavy Melee Weapon; this additional Point is lost if you equip a Heavy Melee Weapon after gaining the Point.\n- +1 Point at the beginning of your Turn if you have dealt Damage to your Opponent since the beginning of your last Turn. \n  - You gain an additional Point if your Opponent has NOT dealt Damage to you since your last Turn.\n\n{{align-text:left\nWhen your Opponent is reduced to 0 Hit Points, you accept their surrender, a minute passes without either of you dealing Damage to the other, or you declare a new Opponent, you lose all Points you have earned.\n:\nYou can expend your Points to carry out Engagements, detailed below. You cannot use the same Engagement more than once per Turn.\n}}",
      "#### Engagements\nThe Engagements available to the Duellist Branch are listed in alphabetical order.\n:"
    ],
    "optionRawSource": "**En Garde (1 Point)** When you expend your Reaction for your Lightning Reflexes or Reposte Press the Attack Option, you may use this Engagement (no Action required) to returning to a guarding stance, refunding use of your Reaction.\n:"
